& [SelectedIntention] is the next dependency-ready authority prerequisite
  + [original_intention] is deterministic capture of changed paths, bytes, tests, event evidence, and independent Observer judgment over an immutable result capsule
  + [purpose] is prevent a mutating worker, its narration, or mutable workspace from certifying its own correctness
  + [required_outcome] is one content-addressed candidate capsule, one separately produced supervisor-test record, and one independent review record
  + [later_consumer] is separately governed Phase3D promotion consideration

& [DelineationFinding] is three distinct Phase3C capabilities
  + [Phase3C1_QuiesceAndSeal] is read-only inspection of the stopped candidate plus write-only publication of a content-addressed immutable capsule outside every repository
  + [Phase3C2_SupervisorTest] is exact supervisor-selected tests against a disposable reconstruction derived only from the capsule
  + [Phase3C3_IndependentReview] is an effect-free decision over the immutable capsule and test record without access to the mutable candidate
  = must: issue separate capability grants, process identities, evidence, and faults for each capability
  - never: let the mutating worker select proof tests, alter the capsule, act as reviewer, or promote its own output

& [SealMeaning] is evidence preservation rather than approval
  + [baseline] is the exact Phase3A base commit and clean receipt
  + [mutation_evidence] is the exact Phase3B MutationRunRecord or quarantine evidence prefix
  + [physical_subject] is the quiescent disposable candidate worktree
  + [capture] is authoritative changed path, type, mode, length, bytes digest, optional bounded bytes, deletion, and repository invariants
  + [capsule] is canonical metadata plus content-addressed blobs and exact upstream evidence digests
  + [signature] attests capture provenance and capsule integrity only
  - never: interpret a valid seal as code correctness, test success, review acceptance, current authority, or promotion permission

& [QuiescenceRequirement] is prior to physical capture
  + [Phase3B_child] is terminal and reaped
  + [descendant_account] is complete or the candidate is quarantined
  + [candidate_identity] still equals the Phase3A receipt
  + [HEAD] and [branch_ref] and [Git_common_dir] are unchanged
  + [index] still represents the exact base tree
  + [capture_window] is bounded and measured
  = must: detect physical state drift across two equivalent inventories or quarantine
  - never: claim a consistent snapshot while a possible writer remains

& [FilesystemCaptureRequirement] is independent of model claims
  + [allowed_changes] are normalized descendants of the Phase3A allowed path set
  + [tracked_change] is reconciled through exact Git observations and direct filesystem hashing
  + [untracked_and_ignored] are explicitly inventoried
  + [special_files] are rejected
  + [links_and_aliases] are rejected unless a later profile separately proves them
  + [Git_metadata] is observed and excluded from candidate content
  + [outside_change_signal] quarantines without cleanup
  = must: preserve deletions and empty files as explicit records

& [ImmutablePublicationRequirement] is separate and bounded
  + [seal_root] is operator-prepared, canonical, empty, outside principal, candidate, Git common directory, temp, and source roots
  + [staging] is a unique private directory under the seal root
  + [publication] is canonical write, fsync where supported, digest verification, atomic rename, and read-only reopening
  + [identity] is derived from the complete capsule manifest digest
  + [collision] succeeds only for byte-identical already-published content
  + [partial_failure] preserves a fault and never names a partial artifact as sealed

& [SupervisorTestRequirement] is independent execution evidence
  + [test_plan] is supervisor-authored before execution with exact executable digests, argument vectors, cwd, environment allowlist, sandbox, network, time, process, output, and artifact budgets
  + [reconstruction] is a fresh disposable workspace created from the exact base and capsule, not the mutable Phase3B worktree
  + [execution] uses direct process launch without shell, hooks, prompts, credentials, or implicit network
  + [record] binds every command, environment, output digest, exit, duration, resources, and reconstruction digest
  + [cleanup] is not part of the proof transition and never erases failed evidence
  - never: treat model-run commands or a worker's final report as supervisor-test proof

& [IndependentReviewRequirement] is a fresh-context judgment
  + [review_input] is only the immutable capsule, verified test record, purpose, criteria, proof obligations, and bounded SOP counsel
  + [reviewer] is not the mutating worker and has no mutable candidate or promotion capability
  + [minimum_reviewer] is a deterministic Observer policy over exact evidence
  + [optional_reviewer] is a separately pinned read-only model turn whose claims remain subordinate to deterministic gates
  + [disposition] is eligible_for_Phase3D_consideration, revise_in_new_candidate, reject, or quarantine
  + [finding] cites exact capsule records, test evidence, criteria, and unresolved uncertainty
  - never: use accept as a synonym for commit, merge, push, deploy, activate, or current authority

& [FaultAndRecoveryRequirement] is evidence-preserving
  + [preseal_fault] leaves the physical candidate quarantined
  + [partial_publication_fault] never produces a valid capsule identity
  + [test_fault] remains attached to the immutable capsule
  + [review_fault] leaves disposition unresolved
  + [operator_disposition] is a later explicit cleanup or retention authority
  - never: reset, clean, delete, rewrite, retry, or reuse the candidate automatically

& [SelectionBoundary] is formation without implementation
  + [inside] is source preservation, canonical and exploded semantics, data design, capability separation, state machine, requirements, justification, feature slice, fault review, and activation blockers
  + [outside] is filesystem capture code, capsule publication, reconstruction, test execution, live reviewer, cleanup, signing-key administration, Git-history mutation, and promotion
  - never: treat this source selection as Phase3C implementation or effect authority
